<article class="env-lemma" id="0434">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0434">Lemma <span data-tag="0434">8.6.6</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. The $2$-category of stacks in setoids over $\mathcal{C}$ has 2-fibre products, and they are described as in Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/0040" data-tag="0040">4.32.3</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is clear from Categories, Lemmas <a href="/tag/0041" data-tag="0041">4.35.7</a> and <a href="/tag/04SB" data-tag="04SB">4.39.4</a> and Lemmas <a href="/tag/02ZJ" data-tag="02ZJ">8.5.2</a> and <a href="/tag/026G" data-tag="026G">8.4.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>